1
00:04:17,048 --> 00:04:20,198
We're here to say goodbye to our brothers and sisters.

2
00:04:21,048 --> 00:04:23,388
To our fathers and mothers.

3
00:04:25,218 --> 00:04:26,238
To our friends.

4
00:04:28,008 --> 00:04:29,768
Our fellow men and women

5
00:04:30,378 --> 00:04:32,528
who set aside their differences...

6
00:04:33,908 --> 00:04:35,218
to fight together...

7
00:04:37,088 --> 00:04:39,048
and die together

8
00:04:39,598 --> 00:04:41,628
so that others might live.

9
00:04:44,028 --> 00:04:45,858
Everyone in this world

10
00:04:46,788 --> 00:04:49,758
owes them a debt that can never be repaid.

11
00:04:50,908 --> 00:04:53,658
It is our duty and our honor

12
00:04:54,278 --> 00:04:56,238
to keep them alive in memory...

13
00:04:58,298 --> 00:04:59,938
for those who come after us...

14
00:05:01,198 --> 00:05:02,938
and those who come after them...

15
00:05:05,038 --> 00:05:07,338
for as long as men draw breath.

16
00:05:10,088 --> 00:05:13,058
They were the shields that guarded the realms of men.

17
00:05:14,948 --> 00:05:17,188
And we shall never see their like again.

18
00:07:49,108 --> 00:07:50,028
To your health.

19
00:08:17,668 --> 00:08:18,698
Have you seen Arya?

20
00:08:21,528 --> 00:08:23,048
You can still smell the burning bodies,

21
00:08:23,048 --> 00:08:24,548
and that's where your head is at.

22
00:08:24,678 --> 00:08:26,878
- I just want to thank her for-- - I'm sure you do.

23
00:08:27,648 --> 00:08:28,698
Look, it's not about that.

24
00:08:28,698 --> 00:08:30,288
Of course it's about that, you twat.

25
00:08:30,408 --> 00:08:31,458
Why shouldn't it be?

26
00:08:31,948 --> 00:08:34,068
The dead are dead. You're not.

27
00:08:48,098 --> 00:08:48,988
Gendry.

28
00:08:52,048 --> 00:08:53,218
That's right, isn't it?

29
00:09:00,008 --> 00:09:00,988
Yes, Your Grace.

30
00:09:01,648 --> 00:09:03,318
You're Robert Baratheon's son.

31
00:09:09,998 --> 00:09:12,038
You are aware he took my family's throne

32
00:09:12,038 --> 00:09:13,558
and tried to have me murdered?

33
00:09:14,448 --> 00:09:17,218
I didn't even know he was my father until after he was dead.

34
00:09:17,938 --> 00:09:20,208
Yes, he's dead.

35
00:09:21,108 --> 00:09:22,358
His brothers are too.

36
00:09:24,348 --> 00:09:26,198
So who's Lord of Storm's End now?

37
00:09:28,618 --> 00:09:29,708
I don't know, Your Grace.

38
00:09:30,668 --> 00:09:31,748
Does anyone?

39
00:09:42,348 --> 00:09:44,578
I think you should be Lord of Storm's End.

40
00:09:50,158 --> 00:09:51,538
I can't be. I'm a bastard.

41
00:09:51,568 --> 00:09:55,738
No, you are Lord Gendry Baratheon of Storm's End,

42
00:09:56,138 --> 00:09:58,528
the lawful son of Robert Baratheon.

43
00:09:59,428 --> 00:10:01,638
Because that is what I have made you.

44
00:10:11,238 --> 00:10:14,718
To Lord Gendry Baratheon of Storm's End.

45
00:10:16,528 --> 00:10:17,268
To Gendry!

46
00:10:17,268 --> 00:10:18,528
Lord Gendry!

47
00:10:19,608 --> 00:10:20,638
Gendry!

48
00:10:21,558 --> 00:10:24,458
- Gendry! - Gendry!

49
00:10:26,088 --> 00:10:27,758
Lord Gendry!

50
00:10:28,868 --> 00:10:29,838
Gendry!

51
00:10:33,408 --> 00:10:34,698
That's easy, isn't it?

52
00:10:37,618 --> 00:10:40,788
- A fitting reward for a hero. - Uh, hold on.

53
00:10:40,788 --> 00:10:44,188
And a Lord of Storm's End who will be forever loyal to you.

54
00:10:44,188 --> 00:10:45,598
- Come, my lord. - See?

55
00:10:46,458 --> 00:10:48,008
You're not the only one who's clever.

56
00:10:58,398 --> 00:11:00,718
I have to go down and get another barrel.

57
00:11:05,048 --> 00:11:07,528
We fought dead things and lived to talk about it.

58
00:11:07,708 --> 00:11:11,018
If this isn't the time to drink, when is?

59
00:11:21,218 --> 00:11:22,618
The last time I saw her,

60
00:11:23,438 --> 00:11:25,688
I told her I'd kill her if I ever saw her again.

61
00:11:26,338 --> 00:11:28,508
- I'm sure you had your reasons. - I did.

62
00:11:29,088 --> 00:11:31,428
- I do. - So did you?

63
00:11:33,698 --> 00:11:34,828
Never got the chance.

64
00:11:35,698 --> 00:11:37,178
She did it to herself.

65
00:11:39,298 --> 00:11:41,248
Or her god did it to her.

66
00:11:43,898 --> 00:11:45,138
Lord of Light.

67
00:11:46,098 --> 00:11:49,218
We play his game for him, we fight his war and win,

68
00:11:49,918 --> 00:11:50,838
and then

69
00:11:51,728 --> 00:11:52,828
he fucks off.

70
00:11:53,248 --> 00:11:56,758
No signs, no blessings. Who knows what he wants?

71
00:11:57,868 --> 00:11:59,948
I don't imagine thinking about that subject

72
00:11:59,948 --> 00:12:02,068
will leave you any happier than before.

73
00:12:02,158 --> 00:12:03,778
And what if I'm not trying to be happy?

74
00:12:06,618 --> 00:12:07,618
Then you're in luck.

75
00:12:10,268 --> 00:12:11,658
We may have defeated them,

76
00:12:12,948 --> 00:12:14,998
but we still have us to contend with.

77
00:12:20,468 --> 00:12:22,368
Thank you. I feel much better.

78
00:12:36,278 --> 00:12:37,288
More ale!

79
00:12:39,778 --> 00:12:40,778
This is clever.

80
00:12:42,718 --> 00:12:44,838
Even better than the saddle I designed for you.

81
00:12:46,628 --> 00:12:48,518
It's the same as the one Daeron Targaryen built

82
00:12:48,518 --> 00:12:51,578
for his crippled nephew 120 years ago.

83
00:12:52,538 --> 00:12:53,608
I liked that one.

84
00:12:54,508 --> 00:12:56,518
You know our history better than anyone.

85
00:12:58,028 --> 00:13:00,078
That will be useful as Lord of Winterfell.

86
00:13:00,988 --> 00:13:02,448
I'm not Lord of Winterfell.

87
00:13:03,108 --> 00:13:05,848
You're the only surviving trueborn son of Ned Stark.

88
00:13:10,848 --> 00:13:11,978
You don't want it.

89
00:13:12,628 --> 00:13:14,778
I don't really want anymore.

90
00:13:16,888 --> 00:13:18,018
I envy you.

91
00:13:21,378 --> 00:13:22,768
You shouldn't envy me.

92
00:13:24,658 --> 00:13:26,238
Mostly I live in the past.

93
00:13:31,978 --> 00:13:33,628
- All of it. - Go on.

94
00:13:33,628 --> 00:13:36,498
- No, not in one go. - Go on. I believe in you.

95
00:13:36,498 --> 00:13:38,278
We have to celebrate our victory.

96
00:13:38,368 --> 00:13:40,588
Vomiting is not celebrating.

97
00:13:40,728 --> 00:13:41,808
Yes, it is.

98
00:13:43,858 --> 00:13:45,328
To the Dragon Queen!

99
00:13:48,088 --> 00:13:50,998
To Arya Stark, the hero of Winterfell!

100
00:13:55,768 --> 00:13:56,708
Drink!

101
00:14:09,588 --> 00:14:10,698
I'm fine!

102
00:14:24,648 --> 00:14:25,808
Your turn.

103
00:14:28,208 --> 00:14:31,158
You are an only child.

104
00:14:32,448 --> 00:14:34,148
- I told you I was. - You didn't.

105
00:14:34,148 --> 00:14:36,608
- I did. - I surmised it.

106
00:14:37,208 --> 00:14:38,178
Drink.

107
00:14:39,618 --> 00:14:40,528
Go again.

108
00:14:41,008 --> 00:14:42,378
Why does he get to go again?

109
00:14:42,388 --> 00:14:43,868
Because it's my game.

110
00:14:44,488 --> 00:14:47,878
You have danced with Renly Baratheon.

111
00:14:49,848 --> 00:14:50,848
No.

112
00:14:50,998 --> 00:14:51,958
Drink.

113
00:14:53,248 --> 00:14:54,338
The other way around!

114
00:14:55,438 --> 00:14:57,488
I saw him riding that thing.

115
00:14:57,688 --> 00:15:00,108
- We all did. - No. No.

116
00:15:00,418 --> 00:15:03,808
I saw him riding that thing.

117
00:15:03,808 --> 00:15:05,898
- That's right, you did. - I did.

118
00:15:06,338 --> 00:15:09,138
That's why we all agreed to follow him.

119
00:15:09,678 --> 00:15:11,748
That's the kind of man he is.

120
00:15:13,638 --> 00:15:14,818
He's little...

121
00:15:15,808 --> 00:15:17,108
...but he's strong.

122
00:15:17,878 --> 00:15:20,438
Strong enough to befriend an enemy

123
00:15:20,628 --> 00:15:22,268
and get murdered for it!

124
00:15:23,018 --> 00:15:25,278
Most people get bloody murdered,

125
00:15:25,418 --> 00:15:26,648
they stay that way.

126
00:15:27,218 --> 00:15:28,308
Not this one.

127
00:15:29,938 --> 00:15:31,738
Yeah, I didn't have much say in that.

128
00:15:32,838 --> 00:15:35,308
He comes back and keeps fighting.

129
00:15:35,488 --> 00:15:39,078
Here, north of the Wall, and then back here again.

130
00:15:39,078 --> 00:15:42,138
He keeps fighting. He keeps fighting.

131
00:15:42,528 --> 00:15:45,088
He climbed on a fucking dragon and fought.

132
00:15:45,558 --> 00:15:48,028
What kind of person climbs on a fucking dragon?

133
00:15:48,068 --> 00:15:50,388
A madman or a king!

134
00:16:06,048 --> 00:16:08,758
- Drink. - Drink.

135
00:16:08,758 --> 00:16:09,718
Drink.

136
00:16:40,478 --> 00:16:41,428
Wrong!

137
00:16:41,638 --> 00:16:43,528
Wrong, wrong, wrong! Drink!

138
00:16:47,128 --> 00:16:50,258
You were married. Before Sansa.

139
00:16:51,188 --> 00:16:52,068
Drink.

140
00:16:57,948 --> 00:16:59,738
You're drinking wine, but you prefer ale!

141
00:16:59,738 --> 00:17:00,648
No!

142
00:17:14,598 --> 00:17:15,618
You're a virgin.

143
00:17:21,598 --> 00:17:23,278
That's a statement about the present.

144
00:17:23,288 --> 00:17:26,038
At no point in the past, up until this very moment,

145
00:17:26,038 --> 00:17:27,468
have you slept with a man.

146
00:17:29,628 --> 00:17:30,538
Or a woman.

147
00:17:37,088 --> 00:17:38,678
I have to piss.

148
00:17:39,068 --> 00:17:42,848
We did it! We faced those icy fucks.

149
00:17:43,138 --> 00:17:45,418
Looked right into their blue eyes,

150
00:17:45,638 --> 00:17:46,788
and here we are.

151
00:17:48,338 --> 00:17:51,468
Now, which one of you cowards shit in my pants?

152
00:17:55,648 --> 00:17:57,788
Please pardon me for a moment.

153
00:18:17,488 --> 00:18:18,448
Drink it!

154
00:18:40,308 --> 00:18:41,768
And after all that,

155
00:18:42,548 --> 00:18:45,388
this fucker comes north and takes her from me.

156
00:18:46,128 --> 00:18:47,938
Just takes her, like that.

157
00:18:49,988 --> 00:18:51,278
I mean it, Clegane.

158
00:18:51,688 --> 00:18:53,158
My heart is broken.

159
00:18:53,418 --> 00:18:54,548
Don't touch me.

160
00:18:54,838 --> 00:18:55,968
You can touch me.

161
00:18:57,448 --> 00:18:59,508
I'm not afraid of wildlings.

162
00:18:59,828 --> 00:19:01,208
Maybe you should be.

163
00:19:05,598 --> 00:19:06,868
Well, Clegane...

164
00:19:08,038 --> 00:19:10,138
it's time to drown our sorrows.

165
00:19:10,638 --> 00:19:12,158
I'm not done with my drink.

166
00:19:13,418 --> 00:19:14,738
You saved the day.

167
00:19:15,408 --> 00:19:16,518
You owe me one.

168
00:19:16,808 --> 00:19:19,978
- Don't forget that. - For the rest of my days.

169
00:19:21,618 --> 00:19:22,768
Are you ready now?

170
00:19:23,438 --> 00:19:24,848
This is my drink.

171
00:19:30,618 --> 00:19:31,468
All right!

172
00:19:40,208 --> 00:19:42,948
She could have made you happy, for a little while.

173
00:19:46,188 --> 00:19:48,278
There's only one thing that'll make me happy.

174
00:19:49,618 --> 00:19:50,558
And what's that?

175
00:19:50,748 --> 00:19:52,468
That's my fucking business.

176
00:19:57,648 --> 00:19:59,548
Used to be you couldn't look at me.

177
00:20:00,648 --> 00:20:02,098
That was a long time ago.

178
00:20:03,138 --> 00:20:05,338
I've seen much worse than you since then.

179
00:20:05,648 --> 00:20:07,148
Yes, I've heard.

180
00:20:07,958 --> 00:20:09,498
Heard you were broken in.

181
00:20:10,528 --> 00:20:12,048
Heard you were broken in rough.

182
00:20:13,308 --> 00:20:14,888
And he got what he deserved.

183
00:20:15,748 --> 00:20:17,148
I gave it to him.

184
00:20:18,348 --> 00:20:19,048
How?

185
00:20:20,698 --> 00:20:21,588
Hounds.

186
00:20:25,618 --> 00:20:27,318
You've changed, Little Bird.

187
00:20:34,068 --> 00:20:35,328
None of it would have happened

188
00:20:35,328 --> 00:20:37,218
if you'd left King's Landing with me.

189
00:20:37,468 --> 00:20:40,398
No Littlefinger, no Ramsay...

190
00:20:41,708 --> 00:20:42,498
none of it.

191
00:20:51,548 --> 00:20:54,158
Without Littlefinger, and Ramsay and the rest,

192
00:20:54,278 --> 00:20:56,588
I would have stayed a Little Bird all my life.

193
00:21:19,338 --> 00:21:20,378
Pour another one.

194
00:21:33,598 --> 00:21:34,298
Don't shoot.

195
00:21:38,288 --> 00:21:40,898
It's nighttime, it's freezing, and everyone's celebrating.

196
00:21:40,988 --> 00:21:42,418
You should be celebrating with them.

197
00:21:43,318 --> 00:21:44,508
I am celebrating.

198
00:21:46,638 --> 00:21:47,778
Yeah, I am too.

199
00:21:50,758 --> 00:21:52,918
I'm not Gendry Rivers anymore.

200
00:21:52,918 --> 00:21:54,718
I'm Gendry Baratheon,

201
00:21:54,718 --> 00:21:56,108
Lord of Storm's End.

202
00:21:56,928 --> 00:21:58,088
By order of the queen.

203
00:22:00,368 --> 00:22:01,668
Congratulations.

204
00:22:05,148 --> 00:22:06,898
I don't know how to be lord of anything.

205
00:22:06,898 --> 00:22:08,588
I hardly know how to use a fork.

206
00:22:08,708 --> 00:22:10,608
All I know is that you're beautiful,

207
00:22:10,608 --> 00:22:11,768
and I love you,

208
00:22:11,778 --> 00:22:13,598
and none of it will be worth anything

209
00:22:13,598 --> 00:22:14,828
if you're not with me.

210
00:22:16,218 --> 00:22:17,188
So be with me.

211
00:22:21,978 --> 00:22:25,238
Be my wife. Be the Lady of Storm's End.

212
00:22:47,448 --> 00:22:49,028
You'll be a wonderful lord,

213
00:22:50,158 --> 00:22:52,458
and any lady would be lucky to have you.

214
00:22:54,328 --> 00:22:55,608
But I'm not a lady.

215
00:22:57,278 --> 00:22:58,388
I never have been.

216
00:23:00,918 --> 00:23:01,828
That's not me.

217
00:23:28,148 --> 00:23:29,178
You didn't drink.

218
00:23:32,388 --> 00:23:34,218
- I didn't drink? - In the game.

219
00:23:35,678 --> 00:23:38,798
- I drank. - In the game. This is Dornish.

220
00:23:41,788 --> 00:23:45,078
This is not the game. This is only drinking.

221
00:23:46,098 --> 00:23:47,048
Suit yourself.

222
00:23:58,138 --> 00:23:59,818
You keep it warm enough in here.

223
00:24:04,108 --> 00:24:06,588
It's the first thing I learnt when I came to the North.

224
00:24:06,928 --> 00:24:08,198
Keep your fire going.

225
00:24:09,038 --> 00:24:10,868
Every time you leave the room, put more wood on.

226
00:24:10,868 --> 00:24:13,718
That's very diligent. Very responsible.

227
00:24:13,718 --> 00:24:14,668
Piss off.

228
00:24:14,668 --> 00:24:16,848
You know the first thing i learned in the North?

229
00:24:17,498 --> 00:24:19,418
I hate the fucking North.

230
00:24:20,658 --> 00:24:21,898
It grows on you.

231
00:24:23,738 --> 00:24:25,738
I don't want things growing on me.

232
00:24:27,528 --> 00:24:29,978
How about Tormund Giantsbane?

233
00:24:30,928 --> 00:24:32,338
Has he grown on you?

234
00:24:34,178 --> 00:24:35,868
He was very sad when you left.

235
00:24:37,608 --> 00:24:39,408
You sound quite jealous.

236
00:24:42,198 --> 00:24:43,418
I do, don't I?

237
00:24:48,818 --> 00:24:50,158
It's bloody hot in here.

238
00:25:00,368 --> 00:25:01,698
Oh, move aside.

239
00:25:07,368 --> 00:25:08,388
What are you doing?

240
00:25:09,498 --> 00:25:10,738
I'm taking your shirt off.

241
00:25:57,968 --> 00:25:59,898
I've never slept with a knight before.

242
00:26:01,518 --> 00:26:03,738
I've never slept with anyone before.

243
00:26:06,168 --> 00:26:08,618
Then you have to drink. Those are the rules.

244
00:26:09,788 --> 00:26:11,158
I told you--

245
00:26:26,658 --> 00:26:27,648
Are you drunk?

246
00:26:32,728 --> 00:26:33,408
No.

247
00:26:38,758 --> 00:26:39,838
Only a little.

248
00:26:50,298 --> 00:26:52,108
I didn't know Ser Jorah well...

249
00:26:53,418 --> 00:26:54,528
but I know this.

250
00:26:56,458 --> 00:26:58,318
If he could have chosen a way to die,

251
00:26:58,318 --> 00:27:00,178
it would have been protecting you.

252
00:27:01,428 --> 00:27:02,408
He loved me.

253
00:27:05,428 --> 00:27:07,048
And I couldn't love him back.

254
00:27:09,618 --> 00:27:10,938
Not the way he wanted.

255
00:27:14,778 --> 00:27:16,378
Not the way I love you.

256
00:27:19,608 --> 00:27:20,698
Is that all right?

257
00:28:00,368 --> 00:28:01,978
I wish you'd never told me.

258
00:28:03,718 --> 00:28:05,668
If I didn't know, I'd be happy right now.

259
00:28:07,908 --> 00:28:09,148
I try to forget.

260
00:28:10,728 --> 00:28:12,168
Tonight I did for a while,

261
00:28:12,178 --> 00:28:15,068
and then I saw them gathered around you.

262
00:28:16,338 --> 00:28:18,238
I saw the way they looked at you.

263
00:28:19,898 --> 00:28:21,028
I know that look.

264
00:28:23,048 --> 00:28:25,908
So many people have looked at me that way, but never here.

265
00:28:26,568 --> 00:28:28,168
Never on this side of the sea.

266
00:28:29,758 --> 00:28:31,048
I told you I don't want it.

267
00:28:31,058 --> 00:28:32,898
It doesn't matter what you want.

268
00:28:33,828 --> 00:28:35,998
You didn't want to be King in the North.

269
00:28:36,158 --> 00:28:38,048
What happens when they demand you press your claim,

270
00:28:38,058 --> 00:28:39,398
and take what is mine?

271
00:28:42,988 --> 00:28:44,428
I'll refuse.

272
00:28:45,168 --> 00:28:47,798
You are my queen. I don't know what else I can say.

273
00:28:47,798 --> 00:28:49,608
You can say nothing.

274
00:28:49,708 --> 00:28:59,708
分析，谁会活到最后？
上知乎搜索「权游谁会死」，给出你的神预测

275
00:28:49,888 --> 00:28:51,238
To anyone, ever.

276
00:28:51,578 --> 00:28:53,508
Never tell them who you really are.

277
00:28:53,678 --> 00:28:56,038
Swear your brother and Samwell Tarly to secrecy,

278
00:28:56,038 --> 00:28:57,328
and tell no one else.

279
00:28:57,728 --> 00:28:59,108
Or it will take on a life of its own

280
00:28:59,108 --> 00:29:00,638
and you won't be able to control it

281
00:29:00,638 --> 00:29:02,138
or what it does to people.

282
00:29:02,218 --> 00:29:04,738
No matter how many times you bend the knee,

283
00:29:04,778 --> 00:29:06,488
no matter what you swear.

284
00:29:12,078 --> 00:29:14,628
I want it to be the way it was between us.

285
00:29:24,598 --> 00:29:26,938
I have to tell Sansa and Arya.

286
00:29:27,068 --> 00:29:30,378
Sansa will want to see me gone

287
00:29:30,378 --> 00:29:32,308
and you on the Iron Throne.

288
00:29:32,728 --> 00:29:33,508
She won't.

289
00:29:34,878 --> 00:29:36,928
She's not the girl you grew up with.

290
00:29:37,728 --> 00:29:39,188
Not after what she's seen,

291
00:29:40,188 --> 00:29:41,978
not after what they've done to her.

292
00:29:46,118 --> 00:29:47,618
I owe them the truth.

293
00:29:48,268 --> 00:29:50,568
Even if the truth destroys us?

294
00:29:51,068 --> 00:29:52,848
- It won't. - It will.

295
00:29:55,358 --> 00:29:57,128
I've never begged for anything...

296
00:29:58,308 --> 00:29:59,728
but I'm begging you.

297
00:30:00,768 --> 00:30:03,648
Don't do this. Please.

298
00:30:10,188 --> 00:30:11,558
You are my queen.

299
00:30:13,168 --> 00:30:15,048
Nothing will change that.

300
00:30:17,858 --> 00:30:19,298
And they are my family.

301
00:30:21,598 --> 00:30:23,118
We can live together.

302
00:30:29,118 --> 00:30:29,918
We can.

303
00:30:32,328 --> 00:30:34,088
I've just told you how.

304
00:31:10,218 --> 00:31:11,368
Half are gone.

305
00:31:15,898 --> 00:31:17,358
The Northmen as well.

306
00:31:23,958 --> 00:31:27,088
And the Golden Company has arrived in King's Landing,

307
00:31:27,088 --> 00:31:29,328
courtesy of the Greyjoy fleet.

308
00:31:29,328 --> 00:31:32,518
The balance has grown distressingly even.

309
00:31:32,888 --> 00:31:35,358
When the people find out what we have done for them,

310
00:31:36,288 --> 00:31:37,228
that we saved them--

311
00:31:37,228 --> 00:31:39,188
Cersei will make sure they don't believe it.

312
00:31:41,468 --> 00:31:42,718
We will hit her hard.

313
00:31:43,178 --> 00:31:45,328
We will rip her out root and stem.

314
00:31:46,848 --> 00:31:49,278
The objective here is to remove Cersei

315
00:31:49,588 --> 00:31:51,488
without destroying King's Landing.

316
00:31:55,528 --> 00:31:58,748
Thankfully, she's losing allies by the day.

317
00:31:59,298 --> 00:32:02,178
Yara Greyjoy has retaken the Iron Islands

318
00:32:02,178 --> 00:32:03,528
in her queen's name.

319
00:32:03,648 --> 00:32:06,438
The new Prince of Dorne pledges his support.

320
00:32:06,438 --> 00:32:08,688
No matter how many lords turn against her,

321
00:32:08,688 --> 00:32:10,358
as long as she sits on the Iron Throne,

322
00:32:10,368 --> 00:32:13,098
she can call herself Queen of the Seven Kingdoms.

323
00:32:15,398 --> 00:32:16,538
We need the capital.

324
00:32:17,608 --> 00:32:19,318
I watched the people of King's Landing

325
00:32:19,318 --> 00:32:21,368
rebel against their king when they were hungry,

326
00:32:21,368 --> 00:32:23,298
and that was before winter began.

327
00:32:23,798 --> 00:32:27,058
Give them the opportunity and they will cast Cersei aside.

328
00:32:28,968 --> 00:32:30,448
We'll surround the city.

329
00:32:31,638 --> 00:32:33,788
If the Iron Fleet tries to ferry in more food,

330
00:32:33,788 --> 00:32:35,318
the dragons will destroy them.

331
00:32:36,148 --> 00:32:38,438
If the Lannisters and the Golden Company attack,

332
00:32:38,448 --> 00:32:40,078
we'll defeat them in the field.

333
00:32:40,288 --> 00:32:42,978
Once the people see that Cersei is our only enemy,

334
00:32:44,048 --> 00:32:45,158
her reign is over.

335
00:32:50,948 --> 00:32:51,598
All right.

336
00:32:52,778 --> 00:32:54,788
The men we have left are exhausted.

337
00:32:55,678 --> 00:32:57,198
Many of them are wounded.

338
00:32:57,378 --> 00:32:58,768
They'll fight better if they have time

339
00:32:58,768 --> 00:33:00,528
to rest and recuperate.

340
00:33:01,698 --> 00:33:03,268
How long do you suggest?

341
00:33:04,688 --> 00:33:05,798
I can't say for certain,

342
00:33:05,798 --> 00:33:07,518
not without talking to the officers.

343
00:33:11,118 --> 00:33:13,808
I came north to fight alongside you

344
00:33:14,098 --> 00:33:16,678
at great cost to my armies and myself.

345
00:33:17,908 --> 00:33:20,448
Now that the time has come to reciprocate,

346
00:33:20,698 --> 00:33:22,198
you want to postpone.

347
00:33:22,578 --> 00:33:25,118
It's not just our people. It's yours.

348
00:33:26,028 --> 00:33:27,168
You want to throw them into a war

349
00:33:27,168 --> 00:33:28,958
they're not ready to fight?

350
00:33:29,038 --> 00:33:30,658
The longer I leave my enemies alone,

351
00:33:30,668 --> 00:33:31,988
the stronger they become.

352
00:33:35,918 --> 00:33:38,788
The Northern forces will honor their promises

353
00:33:39,368 --> 00:33:40,638
and their allegiance

354
00:33:41,148 --> 00:33:43,178
to the Queen of the Seven Kingdoms.

355
00:33:48,648 --> 00:33:50,678
What you command, we will obey.

356
00:33:55,198 --> 00:33:55,938
So...

357
00:33:56,898 --> 00:33:59,038
if all are in agreement...

358
00:34:00,238 --> 00:34:03,118
Jon and Ser Davos will ride down the Kingsroad

359
00:34:03,118 --> 00:34:04,178
with the Northern troops

360
00:34:04,178 --> 00:34:07,088
and the bulk of the remaining Dothraki and Unsullied.

361
00:34:07,088 --> 00:34:09,658
A smaller group of us will ride to White Harbor,

362
00:34:09,658 --> 00:34:11,398
and sail from there to Dragonstone

363
00:34:11,398 --> 00:34:15,038
with our queen and her dragons accompanying us from above.

364
00:34:15,378 --> 00:34:18,098
Ser Jaime has chosen to remain here,

365
00:34:18,098 --> 00:34:20,008
as a guest of the Lady of Winterfell.

366
00:34:23,298 --> 00:34:25,178
We have won the Great War.

367
00:34:26,098 --> 00:34:27,778
Now we will win the Last War.

368
00:34:29,108 --> 00:34:30,918
In all Seven Kingdoms,

369
00:34:31,348 --> 00:34:34,078
men will live without fear and cruelty

370
00:34:35,058 --> 00:34:36,458
under their rightful queen.

371
00:34:49,898 --> 00:34:50,848
We need a word.

372
00:34:55,418 --> 00:34:58,018
You understand we'd all be dead if not for her.

373
00:34:58,598 --> 00:35:00,618
We'd be corpses marching down to King's Landing.

374
00:35:00,618 --> 00:35:02,358
Arya's the one that killed the Night King.

375
00:35:02,358 --> 00:35:04,318
Her men gave their lives defending Winterfell--

376
00:35:04,318 --> 00:35:05,818
And we will never forget them.

377
00:35:05,828 --> 00:35:07,728
That doesn't mean that I want to kneel to someone who--

378
00:35:07,728 --> 00:35:10,628
I swore myself and the North to her cause.

379
00:35:10,628 --> 00:35:11,718
I respect that.

380
00:35:14,858 --> 00:35:16,078
You respect it?

381
00:35:17,248 --> 00:35:18,248
We needed her.

382
00:35:20,298 --> 00:35:23,048
We needed her army, her dragons.

383
00:35:24,748 --> 00:35:25,858
You did the right thing.

384
00:35:27,138 --> 00:35:29,038
And we're doing the right thing telling you

385
00:35:29,208 --> 00:35:30,838
we don't trust your queen.

386
00:35:33,128 --> 00:35:35,108
- You don't know her yet. - I'll never know her.

387
00:35:35,108 --> 00:35:36,418
She's not one of us.

388
00:35:36,548 --> 00:35:38,398
If you only trust the people you grew up with,

389
00:35:38,398 --> 00:35:39,958
you won't make many allies.

390
00:35:39,958 --> 00:35:41,068
That's all right.

391
00:35:41,458 --> 00:35:43,008
I don't need many allies.

392
00:35:43,678 --> 00:35:45,848
- Arya... - We're family.

393
00:35:47,188 --> 00:35:48,338
The four of us.

394
00:35:49,578 --> 00:35:51,148
The last of the Starks.

395
00:35:55,328 --> 00:35:56,778
I've never been a Stark.

396
00:35:57,858 --> 00:35:58,618
You are.

397
00:35:59,708 --> 00:36:02,218
You're just as much Ned Stark's child as any of us.

398
00:36:02,798 --> 00:36:03,838
You're my brother.

399
00:36:04,678 --> 00:36:06,898
Not my half-brother or my bastard brother.

400
00:36:07,978 --> 00:36:08,818
My brother.

401
00:36:17,008 --> 00:36:18,278
It's your choice.

402
00:36:26,038 --> 00:36:27,468
I need to tell you something.

403
00:36:29,808 --> 00:36:33,128
But you have to swear you'll never tell another soul.

404
00:36:36,348 --> 00:36:37,098
What is it?

405
00:36:39,148 --> 00:36:41,338
You have to swear it, before I tell you.

406
00:36:42,658 --> 00:36:44,178
How can I promise to keep a secret

407
00:36:44,178 --> 00:36:45,368
if I don't even know what it is?

408
00:36:45,368 --> 00:36:46,718
Because we're family.

409
00:36:52,278 --> 00:36:53,278
Swear it.

410
00:36:54,488 --> 00:36:55,628
I swear it.

411
00:37:00,608 --> 00:37:01,498
I swear it.

412
00:37:09,698 --> 00:37:10,458
Tell them.

413
00:37:21,628 --> 00:37:23,478
So she's going to stay here with you?

414
00:37:26,608 --> 00:37:29,038
She's sworn to protect the Stark girls, so...

415
00:37:33,048 --> 00:37:34,688
Say something snide.

416
00:37:35,838 --> 00:37:36,858
I'm happy.

417
00:37:36,858 --> 00:37:38,668
I'm happy that you're happy.

418
00:37:41,658 --> 00:37:45,258
I'm happy that you'll finally have to climb for it.

419
00:37:47,118 --> 00:37:50,598
Do you know how long I've waited to tell tall-person jokes?

420
00:37:51,588 --> 00:37:53,208
To climbing mountains.

421
00:37:53,678 --> 00:37:55,238
To climbing mountains.

422
00:37:57,908 --> 00:38:00,198
- What's she like down there? - What?

423
00:38:00,868 --> 00:38:02,848
That's not your concern.

424
00:38:03,098 --> 00:38:05,848
I haven't been with a woman for years.

425
00:38:05,848 --> 00:38:07,058
- Give me a morsel. - You're a dog.

426
00:38:07,058 --> 00:38:09,388
I am the Imp, and I demand to know.

427
00:38:09,388 --> 00:38:10,798
I knew you were fucking her.

428
00:38:12,818 --> 00:38:15,088
A pair of tall, blond toffs.

429
00:38:15,088 --> 00:38:16,688
Must be like looking in the mirror.

430
00:38:16,708 --> 00:38:18,558
Ser Bronn of the Blackwater.

431
00:38:19,948 --> 00:38:21,228
Where's your drink?

432
00:38:22,758 --> 00:38:24,178
What are you-- What are you doing up North?

433
00:38:24,178 --> 00:38:25,368
What are you doing with that?

434
00:38:25,608 --> 00:38:26,458
Oh, this?

435
00:38:27,098 --> 00:38:28,228
This is for you.

436
00:38:29,808 --> 00:38:30,948
For both of you.

437
00:38:30,948 --> 00:38:33,088
You're supposed to be south.

438
00:38:33,248 --> 00:38:35,388
You boys are a pair of gold-plated cunts.

439
00:38:35,388 --> 00:38:36,938
- Do you know that? - That's a bit rude.

440
00:38:36,938 --> 00:38:39,248
Year after year, I've shoveled Lannister shit,

441
00:38:39,248 --> 00:38:41,868
- and what do I have to show? - You're a knight, thanks to me.

442
00:38:41,868 --> 00:38:43,788
Thanks to me. And that title's worth as much

443
00:38:43,788 --> 00:38:45,788
as a blond hair from your brother's ballsack.

444
00:38:45,788 --> 00:38:47,438
Power resides where men believe--

445
00:38:47,438 --> 00:38:49,338
Shut your mouth.

446
00:38:49,728 --> 00:38:51,868
- I'm just trying-- - I've never hit a dwarf before,

447
00:38:51,868 --> 00:38:53,838
but say another word and I will belt you.

448
00:38:53,838 --> 00:38:55,728
See, I don't believe you'd do that, after all--

449
00:38:56,728 --> 00:38:58,238
You couldn't do it on your best day,

450
00:38:58,238 --> 00:38:59,198
you one-handed fuck.

451
00:38:59,198 --> 00:39:00,848
And your best days are long gone.

452
00:39:01,068 --> 00:39:02,778
You broke my nose!

453
00:39:02,778 --> 00:39:04,958
- I did not break your nose. - How do you know?

454
00:39:04,958 --> 00:39:07,158
Because I've been breaking noses since I was your size,

455
00:39:07,158 --> 00:39:09,188
and I know what it sounds like. Now listen.

456
00:39:10,218 --> 00:39:12,298
Your sister offered me Riverrun.

457
00:39:12,788 --> 00:39:14,718
Nice big castle, good lands,

458
00:39:14,718 --> 00:39:16,328
plenty of peasants who do what they're told.

459
00:39:16,328 --> 00:39:18,768
- And you trust Cersei-- - I knew your sister was dead

460
00:39:18,778 --> 00:39:20,848
the second I saw those dragons.

461
00:39:21,278 --> 00:39:23,088
Now, your army may be torn to shit,

462
00:39:23,088 --> 00:39:25,398
but I'd still bet on your Dragon Queen to win.

463
00:39:25,398 --> 00:39:27,568
And it just so happens I'm a betting man.

464
00:39:28,798 --> 00:39:31,848
If Cersei's dead, she can't pay up.

465
00:39:34,428 --> 00:39:36,278
Mmm, that's good. Of course, the odds change

466
00:39:36,278 --> 00:39:38,428
if the Dragon Queen's Hand turns up dead.

467
00:39:38,428 --> 00:39:41,638
Maybe a few of her top generals get picked off one by one.

468
00:39:41,658 --> 00:39:43,678
- All of a sudden... - May I speak?

469
00:39:43,678 --> 00:39:46,318
Why not? Only death will shut you up.

470
00:39:49,438 --> 00:39:52,188
We made a deal long ago. Do you remember?

471
00:39:52,208 --> 00:39:53,278
If anyone offered me money

472
00:39:53,278 --> 00:39:55,268
to kill you, you'd pay me double.

473
00:39:55,858 --> 00:39:57,178
What's double Riverrun?

474
00:39:58,348 --> 00:39:59,278
Highgarden.

475
00:40:01,688 --> 00:40:03,418
You could be Lord of the Reach.

476
00:40:03,418 --> 00:40:06,008
- Highgarden? Are you mad? - It's better than being dead.

477
00:40:06,008 --> 00:40:07,098
He's not going to kill us.

478
00:40:07,098 --> 00:40:08,178
He wouldn't be talking to us if--

479
00:40:12,078 --> 00:40:13,298
The way I see it,

480
00:40:13,538 --> 00:40:16,058
I only need one of the Lannister brothers alive.

481
00:40:16,378 --> 00:40:18,568
Highgarden will never belong to a cutthroat.

482
00:40:18,568 --> 00:40:20,928
No? Who were your ancestors,

483
00:40:20,978 --> 00:40:22,758
the ones who made your family rich?

484
00:40:22,758 --> 00:40:24,248
Fancy lads in silk?

485
00:40:24,338 --> 00:40:26,118
They were fucking cutthroats.

486
00:40:26,348 --> 00:40:28,718
That's how all the great houses started, isn't it?

487
00:40:28,808 --> 00:40:31,388
With a hard bastard who was good at killing people.

488
00:40:31,388 --> 00:40:33,608
Kill a few hundred people, they make you a lord.

489
00:40:33,608 --> 00:40:35,638
Kill a few thousand, they make you king.

490
00:40:35,888 --> 00:40:40,328
And then all your cocksucking grandsons can ruin the family

491
00:40:40,328 --> 00:40:42,068
with their cocksucking ways.

492
00:40:45,578 --> 00:40:46,568
Highgarden.

493
00:40:48,158 --> 00:40:49,378
Give me your word.

494
00:40:51,568 --> 00:40:53,248
You have my word.

495
00:40:54,968 --> 00:40:58,128
None of this means a thing until we take King's Landing.

496
00:40:59,558 --> 00:41:01,298
We ride south in the morning.

497
00:41:01,988 --> 00:41:05,548
We could use an officer with knowledge of the city's defenses.

498
00:41:05,548 --> 00:41:06,358
Oh, no.

499
00:41:06,928 --> 00:41:08,758
No, my fighting days are done.

500
00:41:09,848 --> 00:41:12,528
But I still got a few killing days left, you hear me?

501
00:41:13,538 --> 00:41:15,448
I'll come find you when the war is done.

502
00:41:15,478 --> 00:41:17,558
Till then, don't die.

503
00:41:42,408 --> 00:41:44,668
For fuck's sake.

504
00:41:46,178 --> 00:41:47,088
On your own?

505
00:41:48,628 --> 00:41:49,838
Not anymore.

506
00:41:51,538 --> 00:41:53,098
I don't like crowds.

507
00:41:54,798 --> 00:41:55,598
Me neither.

508
00:41:57,108 --> 00:41:59,348
Why not? They all love you now.

509
00:41:59,658 --> 00:42:00,778
You're the big hero.

510
00:42:01,938 --> 00:42:03,238
Don't like heroes.

511
00:42:05,838 --> 00:42:09,098
It must have felt good sticking a knife in that horned fucker.

512
00:42:10,348 --> 00:42:11,688
Felt better than dying.

513
00:42:15,768 --> 00:42:17,098
You're heading to King's Landing?

514
00:42:18,638 --> 00:42:20,368
I have some unfinished business.

515
00:42:22,188 --> 00:42:22,988
Me too.

516
00:42:29,688 --> 00:42:31,608
I don't plan on coming back.

517
00:42:34,258 --> 00:42:35,198
Neither do I.

518
00:42:37,708 --> 00:42:39,948
Gonna leave me to die again if I get hurt?

519
00:42:42,198 --> 00:42:43,078
Probably.

520
00:43:27,238 --> 00:43:28,078
My lady.

521
00:43:32,768 --> 00:43:35,258
"My lord" is the standard response.

522
00:43:37,758 --> 00:43:38,808
Why her?

523
00:43:43,268 --> 00:43:45,048
You know she loves your brother.

524
00:43:45,518 --> 00:43:47,638
That doesn't mean she'll be a good queen.

525
00:43:48,708 --> 00:43:51,098
You seem determined to dislike her.

526
00:43:53,208 --> 00:43:54,328
A good relationship

527
00:43:54,328 --> 00:43:55,828
between the Iron Throne and the North

528
00:43:55,828 --> 00:43:57,388
has been the core of every peaceful,

529
00:43:57,388 --> 00:43:58,848
prosperous reign we've ever known.

530
00:43:58,848 --> 00:44:00,538
Jon will be Warden of the North,

531
00:44:00,538 --> 00:44:02,988
so a good relationship seems likely.

532
00:44:04,488 --> 00:44:07,608
I don't expect him to spend much time here going forward.

533
00:44:07,608 --> 00:44:09,158
Well, I suppose that's up to him.

534
00:44:13,908 --> 00:44:15,098
Sansa, look at me.

535
00:44:21,198 --> 00:44:22,678
With Jon in the capital,

536
00:44:23,438 --> 00:44:25,568
you'll be the true power in the North.

537
00:44:26,578 --> 00:44:28,268
I'd feel much better about the future

538
00:44:28,268 --> 00:44:29,618
if I left here today believing

539
00:44:29,618 --> 00:44:31,518
that you and Daenerys were allies.

540
00:44:31,528 --> 00:44:34,868
What are you worried about? Jon's taking our army with him.

541
00:44:34,868 --> 00:44:35,578
Your queen still has her dragons--

542
00:44:35,578 --> 00:44:37,738
She's your queen too.

543
00:44:44,798 --> 00:44:46,558
You don't have to be her friend.

544
00:44:47,148 --> 00:44:48,288
But why provoke her?

545
00:44:49,498 --> 00:44:51,468
How is that in the best interest of your family,

546
00:44:51,468 --> 00:44:53,038
- or the North, or--? - You're afraid of her.

547
00:44:56,388 --> 00:45:00,138
Every good ruler needs to inspire a bit of fear.

548
00:45:03,458 --> 00:45:05,328
I don't want Jon to go down there.

549
00:45:05,898 --> 00:45:08,818
The men in my family don't do well in the capital.

550
00:45:09,658 --> 00:45:12,228
No, but as your brother once told me,

551
00:45:12,228 --> 00:45:13,488
he's not a Stark.

552
00:45:19,058 --> 00:45:20,168
Are you all right?

553
00:45:27,208 --> 00:45:29,558
Her people love her, you've seen that.

554
00:45:29,908 --> 00:45:31,598
You've seen how they fight for her.

555
00:45:32,418 --> 00:45:35,448
She wants to make the world a better place.

556
00:45:37,508 --> 00:45:38,838
I believe in her.

557
00:45:54,388 --> 00:45:55,228
Tyrion.

558
00:45:58,578 --> 00:46:00,398
What if there's someone else?

559
00:46:01,378 --> 00:46:02,518
Someone better?

560
00:46:11,348 --> 00:46:13,628
You're not gonna ride the dragon south?

561
00:46:17,178 --> 00:46:18,248
Just a horse.

562
00:46:19,658 --> 00:46:20,848
Rhaegal needs to heal.

563
00:46:20,858 --> 00:46:22,658
He doesn't need me weighing him down.

564
00:46:23,708 --> 00:46:26,198
You weigh as much as two fleas fucking.

565
00:46:27,318 --> 00:46:28,908
I'm taking the Free Folk home.

566
00:46:30,028 --> 00:46:31,818
We've had enough of the south.

567
00:46:33,038 --> 00:46:35,028
The women down here don't like me.

568
00:46:36,958 --> 00:46:38,628
This is the North, you know.

569
00:46:40,478 --> 00:46:42,468
And the Free Folk are welcome to stay.

570
00:46:44,098 --> 00:46:45,348
It isn't home.

571
00:46:46,148 --> 00:46:47,628
We need room to wander.

572
00:46:48,318 --> 00:46:50,138
I'll take them back through Castle Black

573
00:46:50,138 --> 00:46:51,808
as soon as the winter storms pass.

574
00:46:52,358 --> 00:46:53,558
Back where we belong.

575
00:46:57,978 --> 00:46:59,498
It's where he belongs too.

576
00:47:00,488 --> 00:47:02,518
A direwolf has no place in the south.

577
00:47:04,498 --> 00:47:05,648
Will you take him with you?

578
00:47:07,968 --> 00:47:09,258
He'll be happier up there.

579
00:47:10,868 --> 00:47:11,788
So would you.

580
00:47:14,358 --> 00:47:16,018
I wish I was going with you.

581
00:47:21,038 --> 00:47:22,308
This is farewell, then.

582
00:47:24,018 --> 00:47:24,858
You never know.

583
00:47:31,928 --> 00:47:33,788
You've got the North in you.

584
00:47:35,708 --> 00:47:36,958
The real North.

585
00:48:09,688 --> 00:48:12,668
Yes, well, the nights have been getting longer

586
00:48:12,668 --> 00:48:15,638
and there wasn't that much to do in Oldtown.

587
00:48:15,818 --> 00:48:17,948
There's only so many books a person can read, so we--

588
00:48:17,948 --> 00:48:20,338
I'm sure he knows how it happens, Sam.

589
00:48:24,288 --> 00:48:26,898
If it's a boy, we want to name him Jon.

590
00:48:30,058 --> 00:48:31,248
I hope it's a girl.

591
00:48:50,558 --> 00:48:52,348
You're the best friend I ever had.

592
00:48:54,948 --> 00:48:56,048
You too, Sam.

593
00:49:57,748 --> 00:50:00,048
Think of the past 20 years.

594
00:50:00,798 --> 00:50:03,308
The war, the murder, the misery.

595
00:50:03,828 --> 00:50:06,288
All of it because Robert Baratheon loved someone

596
00:50:06,298 --> 00:50:08,098
who didn't love him back.

597
00:50:10,418 --> 00:50:11,548
How many others know?

598
00:50:13,378 --> 00:50:16,148
Including us? Eight.

599
00:50:16,198 --> 00:50:18,178
Well, then it's not a secret anymore.

600
00:50:18,258 --> 00:50:19,688
It's information.

601
00:50:20,188 --> 00:50:23,748
If a handful of people know now, hundreds will know soon.

602
00:50:23,748 --> 00:50:24,648
Then what happens?

603
00:50:24,938 --> 00:50:26,528
She loses the North.

604
00:50:26,818 --> 00:50:29,468
She loses the Vale, Sansa will make sure of that.

605
00:50:29,468 --> 00:50:30,908
No, it's worse than that.

606
00:50:31,108 --> 00:50:33,308
He has the better claim to the throne.

607
00:50:33,868 --> 00:50:35,338
He doesn't want the throne.

608
00:50:36,178 --> 00:50:38,208
I'm not sure it matters what he wants.

609
00:50:39,778 --> 00:50:42,758
The fact is, people are drawn to him.

610
00:50:43,228 --> 00:50:45,268
Wildlings, Northmen.

611
00:50:46,768 --> 00:50:48,098
He's a war hero.

612
00:50:52,648 --> 00:50:53,888
He loves our queen.

613
00:50:56,198 --> 00:50:57,688
And she loves him.

614
00:50:59,908 --> 00:51:02,058
If we marry them, they could rule together.

615
00:51:03,208 --> 00:51:04,438
She's his aunt.

616
00:51:04,438 --> 00:51:05,968
That never stopped a Targaryen before.

617
00:51:05,968 --> 00:51:07,868
No, but Jon grew up in Winterfell.

618
00:51:07,868 --> 00:51:10,188
Is marrying your aunt common in the North?

619
00:51:12,888 --> 00:51:14,378
You know our queen better than I do.

620
00:51:14,378 --> 00:51:16,318
Do you think she wants to share the throne?

621
00:51:17,718 --> 00:51:19,818
She does not like to have her authority questioned.

622
00:51:19,818 --> 00:51:22,818
Something she has in common with every monarch who ever lived.

623
00:51:24,078 --> 00:51:25,998
I worry about her state of mind.

624
00:51:26,158 --> 00:51:28,038
We are advisors to the queen.

625
00:51:28,038 --> 00:51:31,238
Worrying about her state of mind is our job.

626
00:51:39,308 --> 00:51:41,118
We still have to take King's Landing.

627
00:51:42,458 --> 00:51:44,478
Maybe Cersei will win and kill us all.

628
00:51:45,218 --> 00:51:46,848
That would solve our problems.

629
00:53:50,828 --> 00:53:53,428
Get to the skiff. Now!

630
00:53:55,678 --> 00:53:56,598
Spears!

631
00:53:56,938 --> 00:53:58,318
They're coming round again!

632
00:54:07,438 --> 00:54:08,308
Go!

633
00:54:32,528 --> 00:54:33,788
Go! Go!

634
00:55:10,178 --> 00:55:11,098
Missandei?

635
00:55:12,888 --> 00:55:13,988
Missandei!

636
00:55:20,028 --> 00:55:21,428
Missandei!

637
00:55:26,848 --> 00:55:28,878
Our message was well-received, then?

638
00:55:28,918 --> 00:55:31,528
Your people have heard the Usurper is coming.

639
00:55:32,178 --> 00:55:34,428
They are grateful for your protection

640
00:55:34,428 --> 00:55:36,708
within the walls of the Red Keep.

641
00:55:39,018 --> 00:55:40,588
You're certain about the dragon?

642
00:55:41,508 --> 00:55:43,808
I saw it sink beneath the waves.

643
00:55:44,018 --> 00:55:45,778
That must have been glorious.

644
00:55:48,188 --> 00:55:50,418
The glory is yours, my queen.

645
00:55:51,738 --> 00:55:54,108
When the war is won, the Lion shall rule the land,

646
00:55:54,108 --> 00:55:55,748
the Kraken shall rule the sea...

647
00:55:57,418 --> 00:56:00,188
and our child shall one day rule them all.

648
00:56:17,168 --> 00:56:18,768
She's coming for you.

649
00:56:20,078 --> 00:56:21,298
Of course she is.

650
00:56:24,168 --> 00:56:25,878
Keep the gates open.

651
00:56:26,418 --> 00:56:28,458
If she wants to take the castle, she'll have to murder

652
00:56:28,458 --> 00:56:30,788
thousands of innocent people first.

653
00:56:37,288 --> 00:56:39,398
So much for "The Breaker of Chains."

654
00:56:53,488 --> 00:56:55,618
We will storm the city, my queen.

655
00:56:55,848 --> 00:56:58,828
We will kill your enemies. All of them.

656
00:56:59,098 --> 00:57:00,068
Your Grace.

657
00:57:01,888 --> 00:57:05,788
I promised you I would look you in the eye and speak directly

658
00:57:05,788 --> 00:57:08,238
if I ever thought you were making a mistake.

659
00:57:11,358 --> 00:57:13,868
This is a mistake.

660
00:57:16,848 --> 00:57:19,308
You saw my child fall from the sky.

661
00:57:20,758 --> 00:57:22,208
They took Missandei.

662
00:57:23,178 --> 00:57:25,278
Cersei needs to be destroyed,

663
00:57:25,278 --> 00:57:29,168
but if we attack King's Landing with Drogon and the Unsullied

664
00:57:29,168 --> 00:57:30,458
and the Dothraki,

665
00:57:30,458 --> 00:57:33,438
tens of thousands of innocents will die.

666
00:57:33,488 --> 00:57:36,528
That is why Cersei is bringing them into the Red Keep.

667
00:57:38,118 --> 00:57:40,948
These are the people you came here to protect.

668
00:57:41,548 --> 00:57:43,178
I beg you, Your Grace.

669
00:57:43,178 --> 00:57:46,348
Do not destroy the city you came to save.

670
00:57:47,108 --> 00:57:50,698
Do not become what you have always struggled to defeat.

671
00:57:55,868 --> 00:57:58,188
Do you believe we're here for a reason, Lord Varys?

672
00:58:02,298 --> 00:58:04,978
I'm here to free the world from tyrants.

673
00:58:06,258 --> 00:58:07,698
That is my destiny...

674
00:58:09,178 --> 00:58:11,818
and I will serve it, no matter the cost.

675
00:58:19,468 --> 00:58:21,928
It could be a fortnight before Jon and the allied armies

676
00:58:21,928 --> 00:58:23,308
make it to King's Landing.

677
00:58:24,348 --> 00:58:27,098
In the meantime, demand Cersei surrender.

678
00:58:27,108 --> 00:58:29,858
Offer her her life in exchange for the throne.

679
00:58:32,328 --> 00:58:34,658
If there's a chance to avoid the coming slaughter,

680
00:58:34,658 --> 00:58:36,248
we should make the effort.

681
00:58:37,058 --> 00:58:39,548
Speaking to Cersei will not prevent a slaughter.

682
00:58:42,148 --> 00:58:43,988
But perhaps it's good the people see

683
00:58:43,988 --> 00:58:47,438
that Daenerys Stormborn made every effort to avoid bloodshed,

684
00:58:47,758 --> 00:58:50,098
and Cersei Lannister refused.

685
00:58:52,218 --> 00:58:53,468
They should know whom to blame

686
00:58:53,468 --> 00:58:55,158
when the sky falls down upon them.

687
00:59:09,648 --> 00:59:12,288
I've served tyrants most of my life.

688
00:59:13,218 --> 00:59:15,848
They all talk about destiny.

689
00:59:16,778 --> 00:59:20,008
She's a girl who walked into a fire with three stones

690
00:59:20,008 --> 00:59:22,268
and walked out with three dragons.

691
00:59:22,678 --> 00:59:25,228
How could she not believe in destiny?

692
00:59:25,598 --> 00:59:27,398
Perhaps that's the problem.

693
00:59:27,688 --> 00:59:28,838
Her life has convinced her

694
00:59:28,838 --> 00:59:30,678
that she was sent here to save us all.

695
00:59:30,678 --> 00:59:32,538
And how do you know she wasn't?

696
00:59:34,758 --> 00:59:37,008
Then there's the problem of Jon Snow.

697
00:59:43,298 --> 00:59:45,908
Perhaps it's actually a solution.

698
00:59:47,958 --> 00:59:48,998
You know them both.

699
00:59:48,998 --> 00:59:51,918
Tell me, who do you think would make a better ruler?

700
00:59:57,548 --> 00:59:59,268
He doesn't want the throne.

701
00:59:59,928 --> 01:00:02,008
That's why he bent the knee.

702
01:00:02,598 --> 01:00:04,108
Have you considered the best ruler

703
01:00:04,108 --> 01:00:06,098
might be someone who doesn't want to rule?

704
01:00:06,668 --> 01:00:08,628
We're discussing treason.

705
01:00:10,148 --> 01:00:11,648
Don't pretend you haven't thought about it.

706
01:00:11,658 --> 01:00:14,508
Of course I've thought about it. Thoughts aren't treason.

707
01:00:17,138 --> 01:00:21,298
He's temperate and measured. He's a man,

708
01:00:21,578 --> 01:00:24,028
which makes him more appealing to the lords of Westeros,

709
01:00:24,028 --> 01:00:25,828
whose support we are going to need.

710
01:00:26,638 --> 01:00:27,928
Joffrey was a man.

711
01:00:28,328 --> 01:00:30,188
I don't think a cock is a true qualification,

712
01:00:30,188 --> 01:00:31,468
as I'm sure you'd agree.

713
01:00:31,658 --> 01:00:33,688
And he's the heir to the throne.

714
01:00:33,688 --> 01:00:37,048
Yes, because he's a man. Cocks are important, I'm afraid.

715
01:00:40,358 --> 01:00:42,548
What about my earlier proposal?

716
01:00:43,658 --> 01:00:45,958
They could rule together as king and queen.

717
01:00:47,238 --> 01:00:48,968
She's too strong for him.

718
01:00:49,788 --> 01:00:53,348
She'd bend him to her will, as she already has.

719
01:00:53,348 --> 01:00:55,788
He could temper her worst impulses.

720
01:00:56,558 --> 01:00:57,668
As you have?

721
01:01:01,628 --> 01:01:03,068
You're drinking quite a lot.

722
01:01:06,148 --> 01:01:09,358
A Targaryen father and a Stark mother.

723
01:01:10,128 --> 01:01:12,998
Jon's the one man alive who might actually be able

724
01:01:13,008 --> 01:01:14,828
to keep the North in the Seven Kingdoms.

725
01:01:14,828 --> 01:01:16,378
How many kings and queens have you served?

726
01:01:16,378 --> 01:01:17,718
Five? Six? I've lost count.

727
01:01:17,718 --> 01:01:19,888
- You've always known my reasons. - At a certain point,

728
01:01:19,888 --> 01:01:21,628
you choose a person you believe in,

729
01:01:21,628 --> 01:01:22,998
and you fight for that person.

730
01:01:22,998 --> 01:01:25,218
Even if you know it's a mistake?

731
01:01:26,948 --> 01:01:28,598
I believe in our queen.

732
01:01:31,168 --> 01:01:32,798
She'll make the right choice.

733
01:01:35,178 --> 01:01:38,108
With the help of her loyal advisors.

734
01:01:41,718 --> 01:01:43,898
You know where my loyalty stands.

735
01:01:44,178 --> 01:01:46,468
You know I will never betray the realm.

736
01:01:46,468 --> 01:01:47,808
What is the realm?

737
01:01:48,128 --> 01:01:50,008
A vast continent, home to millions of people,

738
01:01:50,008 --> 01:01:52,148
most of whom don't care who sits on the Iron Throne.

739
01:01:52,148 --> 01:01:54,178
Millions of people, many of whom will die

740
01:01:54,178 --> 01:01:56,528
if the wrong person sits on that throne.

741
01:01:57,048 --> 01:01:58,218
We don't know their names,

742
01:01:58,218 --> 01:02:00,018
but they're just as real as you and I.

743
01:02:00,018 --> 01:02:01,478
They deserve to live.

744
01:02:01,478 --> 01:02:03,758
They deserve food for their children.

745
01:02:07,238 --> 01:02:11,218
I will act in their interest, no matter the personal cost.

746
01:02:13,598 --> 01:02:15,798
So, what happens to her?

747
01:02:24,058 --> 01:02:25,118
Please.

748
01:02:27,518 --> 01:02:28,698
Don't.

749
01:02:33,398 --> 01:02:35,568
I've spoken as honestly as I can.

750
01:02:37,438 --> 01:02:39,538
Each of us has a choice to make.

751
01:02:41,118 --> 01:02:43,188
I pray we choose wisely.

752
01:02:55,088 --> 01:02:56,828
I'm just about to start it.

753
01:02:56,958 --> 01:02:57,918
Good luck.

754
01:02:58,588 --> 01:03:00,478
Protect shell right up to the wall.

755
01:03:00,478 --> 01:03:01,958
All right, I'll put another one on it.

756
01:03:02,088 --> 01:03:03,518
He's headed down to the cellar.

757
01:03:03,788 --> 01:03:04,938
I'll need a cart over here.

758
01:03:06,158 --> 01:03:07,258
That's it, thanks.

759
01:03:07,398 --> 01:03:08,498
Thank you.

760
01:03:09,228 --> 01:03:10,648
It's really heavy, mind you.

761
01:03:10,738 --> 01:03:12,088
We need some more water.

762
01:03:12,258 --> 01:03:13,418
Take it down there!

763
01:03:18,588 --> 01:03:20,508
...as are the rest of her advisors.

764
01:03:23,048 --> 01:03:24,178
What happened?

765
01:03:29,898 --> 01:03:33,238
Euron Greyjoy ambushed Queen Daenerys and her fleet.

766
01:03:34,558 --> 01:03:37,258
One of the dragons was killed, several ships destroyed,

767
01:03:37,258 --> 01:03:38,708
Missandei captured.

768
01:03:41,428 --> 01:03:44,758
I always wanted to be there when they execute your sister.

769
01:03:45,718 --> 01:03:47,468
Seems like I won't get the chance.

770
01:04:55,078 --> 01:04:56,968
They're going to destroy that city.

771
01:04:58,618 --> 01:04:59,768
You know they will.

772
01:05:00,688 --> 01:05:02,448
Have you ever run away from a fight?

773
01:05:04,578 --> 01:05:07,228
You're not like your sister. You're not.

774
01:05:07,518 --> 01:05:09,058
You're better than she is.

775
01:05:09,348 --> 01:05:11,738
You're a good man and you can't save her.

776
01:05:11,848 --> 01:05:13,318
You don't need to die with her.

777
01:05:14,228 --> 01:05:15,328
Stay here.

778
01:05:17,258 --> 01:05:18,448
Stay with me.

779
01:05:20,318 --> 01:05:21,448
Please.

780
01:05:23,398 --> 01:05:24,398
Stay.

781
01:05:31,008 --> 01:05:32,448
You think I'm a good man?

782
01:05:37,738 --> 01:05:40,258
I pushed a boy out a tower window,

783
01:05:40,258 --> 01:05:41,598
crippled him for life

784
01:05:42,578 --> 01:05:43,678
for Cersei.

785
01:05:46,758 --> 01:05:49,498
I strangled my cousin with my own hands

786
01:05:50,568 --> 01:05:52,408
just to get back to Cersei.

787
01:05:55,718 --> 01:05:57,138
I would have murdered

788
01:05:57,578 --> 01:06:00,638
every man, woman and child in Riverrun

789
01:06:01,398 --> 01:06:02,518
for Cersei.

790
01:06:11,448 --> 01:06:12,668
She's hateful.

791
01:06:15,088 --> 01:06:16,328
And so am I.

792
01:08:51,358 --> 01:08:52,458
My lord.

793
01:08:55,898 --> 01:08:58,798
Queen Daenerys demands Cersei's unconditional surrender

794
01:08:58,988 --> 01:09:01,848
and the immediate release of Missandei of Naath.

795
01:09:03,378 --> 01:09:07,698
Queen Cersei demands Daenerys's unconditional surrender.

796
01:09:07,928 --> 01:09:11,548
If she refuses, Missandei of Naath will die here and now.

797
01:09:13,348 --> 01:09:14,428
Qyburn...

798
01:09:15,878 --> 01:09:17,498
you're a rational man.

799
01:09:18,038 --> 01:09:20,458
Or so I flatter myself, my lord.

800
01:09:20,788 --> 01:09:22,118
We have a chance here,

801
01:09:23,548 --> 01:09:26,728
perhaps our last chance, to avoid carnage.

802
01:09:26,998 --> 01:09:27,928
Yes.

803
01:09:29,748 --> 01:09:30,778
Help me.

804
01:09:32,158 --> 01:09:34,338
I don't want to see this city burn.

805
01:09:35,288 --> 01:09:38,778
I don't want to hear the screams of children burning alive.

806
01:09:40,358 --> 01:09:43,188
No, it is not a pleasant sound.

807
01:09:45,448 --> 01:09:47,788
I-- I don't want to hear it.

808
01:09:48,718 --> 01:09:50,478
Help me save this city.

809
01:09:52,248 --> 01:09:54,688
My lord, I am only a mouthpiece for our queen.

810
01:09:54,788 --> 01:09:55,958
Your queen.

811
01:09:56,718 --> 01:09:58,858
Cersei is Queen of the Seven Kingdoms.

812
01:09:58,858 --> 01:10:00,138
You are her subject.

813
01:10:00,138 --> 01:10:01,708
Her reign is over.

814
01:10:02,348 --> 01:10:05,108
You understand this. Help her understand it.

815
01:10:05,118 --> 01:10:07,498
We understand nothing of the sort.

816
01:10:08,728 --> 01:10:11,278
Your queen's last dragon is vulnerable.

817
01:10:11,478 --> 01:10:14,008
Your armies are battle-weary and depleted,

818
01:10:14,408 --> 01:10:17,488
while ours have been reinforced with the Golden Compan--

819
01:10:35,478 --> 01:10:36,698
Ready!

820
01:10:37,788 --> 01:10:38,748
Nock!

821
01:10:41,638 --> 01:10:42,708
Draw!

822
01:11:49,228 --> 01:11:52,008
I know you don't care about your people.

823
01:11:53,908 --> 01:11:55,088
Why should you?

824
01:11:57,328 --> 01:12:00,138
They hate you and you hate them.

825
01:12:06,338 --> 01:12:08,048
But you're not a monster.

826
01:12:10,728 --> 01:12:11,878
I know this.

827
01:12:14,188 --> 01:12:16,428
I know this because I've seen it.

828
01:12:21,078 --> 01:12:23,028
You've always loved your children.

829
01:12:25,338 --> 01:12:26,638
More than yourself,

830
01:12:27,728 --> 01:12:28,948
more than Jaime...

831
01:12:31,988 --> 01:12:33,238
more than anything.

832
01:12:36,418 --> 01:12:37,548
I beg you.

833
01:12:40,418 --> 01:12:43,348
If not for yourself, then for your child.

834
01:12:47,448 --> 01:12:48,738
Your reign is over,

835
01:12:49,718 --> 01:12:52,408
but that doesn't mean your life has to end.

836
01:12:55,978 --> 01:12:58,278
It doesn't mean your baby has to die.

837
01:13:46,788 --> 01:13:49,738
If you have any last words, now is the time.

838
01:14:14,958 --> 01:14:16,168
Dracarys.

839
01:14:26,108 --> 01:14:27,048
No.

